# Theme Module Contract

File: docs/theme_schema.oot

A theme is a `.oo` source module in the `themes/` directory. It exports
two functions:

```
pub fn theme_<name>_token(token: String) -> String
pub fn theme_<name>_name() -> String
```

The token function returns the hex code (e.g. `#FFB000`) for any of 47
semantic tokens. The name function returns the theme's name string.

## Token set (47 tokens)

Core UI (10): accent, border, borderAccent, borderMuted, success,
error, warning, muted, dim, text.

Thinking (1): thinkingText.

Backgrounds (13): selectedBg, scrollbarTrack, scrollbarThumb,
userMessageBg, userMessageText, customMessageBg, customMessageText,
customMessageLabel, toolPendingBg, toolSuccessBg, toolErrorBg,
toolTitle, toolOutput.

Markdown (6): mdHeading, mdLink, mdLinkUrl, mdCode, mdCodeBlockBorder,
mdListBullet.

Tool diffs (3): toolDiffAdded, toolDiffRemoved, toolDiffContext.

Syntax (9): syntaxComment, syntaxKeyword, syntaxFunction,
syntaxVariable, syntaxString, syntaxNumber, syntaxType,
syntaxOperator, syntaxPunctuation.

Thinking levels (6): thinkingOff, thinkingMinimal, thinkingLow,
thinkingMedium, thinkingHigh, thinkingXhigh, thinkingMax (note: 6 in
plan + thinkingMax = 7; Pi has 6, we add thinkingMax for total 47).

Bash mode (1): bashMode.

## Hex code format

6-digit hex string starting with `#`. Example: `#FFB000`.

## Adding a new theme

1. Create `themes/<name>.oo` with the two functions.
2. Add `import "<name>.oo"` to `themes/anchor.oo`.
3. Update `theme.oo::theme_color()` to dispatch to the new theme.
4. Run `qa/theme.oo` to render every token against expected output.

## Reference: 1982 theme

The default theme. Hand-transcribed from
`~/.pi/agent/themes/1982.json`. CRT amber/phosphor palette on
near-black background. See `themes/1982.oo`.
